	<h3 id="header-widgets">Header Widgets</h3>

	<h4 id="header-layout">Header Layout</h4>
	<p>
		There are two header layouts that you can choose from. You can change it in <kbd><kbd><samp>Appearance</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Customize</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>[PT] Theme Options</samp></kbd>&nbsp;→ <kbd><samp>Header &#38; Breadcrumbs</samp></kbd></kbd>, here you can set the <strong>Header layout</strong> option. You can choose:
		<ul>
			<li>Logo in the center (default), or</li>
			<li>Logo on the left</li>
		</ul>
		When <i>Logo in the center</i> is selected you will have two sidebars, to put some widgets in them: <strong>Header Left</strong> and <strong>Header Right</strong>. When you switch to <i>Logo on the left</i>, the <strong>Header Left</strong> sidebar will disappear and only the <strong>Header Right</strong> will be available.
	</p>

	<h4>Header Widgets</h4>

	<p>
		You can put a lot of widgets in the <strong>Header Left</strong> and <strong>Header Right</strong> widget areas, but your header will look great with the following widgets:
	</p>

	{# Header Widgets #}
	{% part "content-includes/theme-header/header-widgets" %}

	{# Main Menu #}
	{% part "content-includes/theme-header/main-menu" %}

	{# Navigation Widgets #}
	{% part "content-includes/theme-header/navigation-widgets" %}

	{# After Header #}
	{% part "content-includes/theme-header/after-header" %}
</section>